  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Assessing Aesthetic Completeness**\n\nI\'ve determined the visual setup is finalized. Dark charcoal `#111318` provides the foundation, paired with vibrant cyan `#00d4ff` for key elements. Muted gold `#c9a84c` adds subtle accents throughout. DM Mono, implemented via `font-mono`, has been correctly applied to all timers and labels.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have completely redesigned the visual language of the application to match the high-performance, \"war room\" competition tool aesthetic. \n\nHere\'s an overview of the changes applied:\n- **Atmosphere & Palette:** Set the background to dark charcoal (`#111318`) with a subtle grid-dot overlay created purely using CSS. Muted gold (`#c9a84c`) is utilized for tags, labels, and accents while electric cyan (`#00d4ff`) acts as the sharp primary interactive and active color.\n- **Typography:** Imported Google Fonts **\"Syne\"** for the global body/headings and **\"DM Mono\"** for all timers, labels, tags, and data. These were mapped directly to your standard and `font-mono` styles.\n- **Card Stylings:** Applied `war-card` global CSS class to all sections and input/interactive regions. This provides a precise 1-pixel border in `rgba(255,255,255,0.08)` and adds a subtle internal blue/white glow on hover.\n- **Sharp Geometry:** Systematically removed all occurrences of large border radii (`rounded-xl`, `rounded-lg`, and `rounded-md`) across the entire codebase substituting them with sharp `rounded-sm`.\n- **Transitions:** Subbed out the former bottom-fade entrance with a custom `slide-in-left` CSS animation on a 150ms ease-out curve. Sections snap in place from the left rapidly, echoing the performance tone of a Bloomberg terminal-like tool.\n\nThe app\'s environment now looks like a precise and tactical control room."
